# ops/Caddyfile — Step 5.1 (DEPLOYMENT_PLAN.md)
#
# Automatic HTTPS for the Step-1.9 Azure VM's DNS label. Caddy provisions
# and renews the Let's Encrypt certificate on its own — just naming the
# domain as the site address (below) is enough; no separate `tls` directive
# needed unless that default ever needs overriding.
#
# {$DNS_LABEL} is Caddy's own environment-variable substitution (distinct
# from docker compose's ${VAR} substitution in docker-compose.prod.yml) —
# it reads the DNS_LABEL env var docker-compose.prod.yml's `caddy` service
# passes into this container, so the same file works without editing
# regardless of whose Azure DNS label is actually in use.
#
# Routing: ONE public domain, split by path —
#   /api/*  -> backend (path prefix stripped before proxying, so the
#              backend's own routes — /users, /jobs, /generate, etc. — never
#              need to know this prefix exists at all)
#   everything else -> frontend (the built React app)
# frontend/src/shared/services/api.js's REACT_APP_API_URL is set to
# "https://<label>/api" at build time (docker-compose.prod.yml) specifically
# to match this split — every axios call already includes /api, so Caddy's
# strip-then-forward here is the other half of that contract.
{$DNS_LABEL} {
	handle_path /api/* {
		reverse_proxy backend:8000
	}

	handle {
		reverse_proxy frontend:80
	}
}
